@startuml Training Sequence
!theme plain

title Model Training Sequence Diagram

actor Client
participant "Model API\n:8001" as ModelAPI
participant "Backend API\n:8000" as BackendAPI
database "SQLite DB" as Database
participant "Random Forest\nModel" as Model

Client -> ModelAPI: POST /train\n(Optional: X-Database-Name header)
activate ModelAPI

ModelAPI -> BackendAPI: GET /api/health\n(Check backend status)
activate BackendAPI
BackendAPI --> ModelAPI: 200 OK
deactivate BackendAPI

ModelAPI -> BackendAPI: GET /training\n?limit=1000&offset=0\nHeader: X-Database-Name
activate BackendAPI
BackendAPI -> Database: SELECT * FROM csv_data\nWHERE T = 'training'
activate Database
Database --> BackendAPI: Training Data Rows
deactivate Database
BackendAPI --> ModelAPI: JSON Response\n{data: [...], total_rows: N}
deactivate BackendAPI

ModelAPI -> ModelAPI: Extract Features\nParse JSON Data\nCreate DataFrame

ModelAPI -> ModelAPI: Split Features & Labels\n(label: 0=safe, 1=unsafe)

ModelAPI -> Model: Train RandomForestClassifier\nn_estimators=100
activate Model
Model --> ModelAPI: Trained Model
deactivate Model

ModelAPI -> ModelAPI: Save Model\nmodels/random_forest_model.pkl\nSave Metadata (JSON)

ModelAPI --> Client: 200 OK\n{status: "success",\naccuracy: X.XX,\nmodel_path: "..."}
deactivate ModelAPI

@enduml
